The new native worker backend descriptor exports:

```js
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_ADAPTER_CONTRACT_VERSION
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_KIND
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_ADAPTER_ID
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_ADAPTER_VERSION
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_ADAPTER_STATUS
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_CAPABILITIES
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_SERVICES
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_RESULT_SCHEMA
NATIVE_WORKER_BACKEND_RESULT_OUTPUT_FIELDS
createNativeWorkerBackendAdapterDefinition()
validateNativeWorkerBackendAdapterDefinition(adapter)
assertNativeWorkerBackendAdapterDefinition(adapter)
```

The canonical descriptor is:

```js
{
    adapterId: "native-worker.default",
    backendKind: "nativeWorkerBackend",
    version: "v1",
    status: "contract-only",
    capabilities: ["text.generate"],
    services: ["text.generate.default"],
    result: {
        schema: "text.generate.result.v1",
        outputFields: ["text"],
        streamingDeltas: "supported",
        errorNormalization: "supported"
    },
    requirements: {
        streaming: "supported",
        cancellation: "supported",
        timeout: "supported"
    },
    compatibility: {
        backendKind: "nativeWorkerBackend",
        modelBundleRequired: true,
        hardwareProfileRequired: true
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Contract behavior

The generic backend adapter contract remains the shared descriptor/registry/plan surface.

The native-worker-specific contract is stricter than the generic contract and validates the canonical native worker descriptor:

```text
adapterId must be native-worker.default
backendKind must be nativeWorkerBackend
version must be v1
status must be contract-only
capabilities must be exactly text.generate
services must be exactly text.generate.default
result schema/output/support metadata must match the text.generate result contract
streaming/cancellation/timeout support must remain supported
modelBundleRequired must be true
hardwareProfileRequired must be true
```

Invalid descriptor cases are constructed in tests manually. The production factory does not accept arbitrary override payloads.

---

## 5. Architecture boundaries preserved

This branch does not:

```text
change runtime.mjs public APIs
import or call workerBridge
import llama_worker modules
load models
spawn workers or child processes
execute backend adapters
call capability services
modify scheduler/request/stream behavior
change lifecycle/init/reset/shutdown behavior
change configOverride behavior
add request-time raw model path support
add default alias routing
add multimodal/vision/video execution
add memory/storage backend behavior
implement Cognitive Graph Runtime behavior
```

Tests validate the intended architecture. The architecture was not shaped around tests.

